  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#10877;</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#10877;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\"><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>:</mo><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\"><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. Then,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "is an empty set",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "contains exactly two elements",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "contains exactly three elements",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "is an infinite set",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;represents two concentric circles with centre&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\"><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;represents a circle with centre&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and radius&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0092_70fd313c4e47.png\" style=\"width: 201px; height: 200px;\" /></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;represents the region between the concentric circles with centre&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Set <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> contains all points on minor arc&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></math>&nbsp;of&nbsp;the circle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>.</p><p>Hence,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;has infinite elements.</p>"
  }
